    "text": "To determine Betty's height in feet, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find Carter's height:**\n   Carter is twice as tall as his 24-inch dog.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Carter's height} = 2 \\times 24 \\text{ inches} = 48 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find Betty's height:**\n   Betty is 12 inches shorter than Carter.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Betty's height} = 48 \\text{ inches} - 12 \\text{ inches} = 36 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Convert Betty's height to feet:**\n   There are 12 inches in a foot.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Betty's height in feet} = \\frac{36 \\text{ inches}}{12 \\text{ inches/foot}} = 3 \\text{ feet}\n   \\]\n\nThus, Betty's height is \\(\\boxed{3}\\) feet.",
